{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785098153,"nonce":"flCqZQbwrTERMGn5jvGEbleYhs4=","title":"**Found by the live kube tier while landing ADR-0061 s3-feed. Not an s3-feed","message":"regression — s7's, and measured rather than reasoned about.**\n\n`crates/scarab-executor-k8s/tests/cluster.rs::workspace_flows_from_a_to_b_through_the_cas`\nasserts restart determinism: two attempts of a step that writes identical content\nmust produce the same CAS root. It now fails. Both roots, fetched from the warm\ntier:\n\n    6ab25ad8… [{\"name\":\"out.txt\",\"target\":{\"Blob\":\"d112afe6…\"},\"mode\":420,\"mtime_ms\":1785098063000}]\n    93722441… [{\"name\":\"out.txt\",\"target\":{\"Blob\":\"d112afe6…\"},\"mode\":420,\"mtime_ms\":1785098073000}]\n\nSame blob. Same mode. mtime 10 seconds apart. Different root.\n\nADR-0061's s7 note says this is correct in itself — \"a *tree* hash does move with\nan mtime, which is correct, since two checkouts with different timestamps are\ndifferent workspaces to every tool that compares them\" — and it is. What it does\nnot reckon with is the consequence for **ADR-0027**, whose content-addressed\ninvalidation is built on the opposite property:\n\n- a producer re-run can now NEVER yield its previous root, because it writes files\n  at a new wall-clock time;\n- so every downstream step's skip-if-unchanged signature always changes;\n- so \"smart never means mysterious\" degrades to \"nothing is ever skipped\", and the\n  restart-semantics feature is dead code on the k8s path rather than wrong. Which\n  is the better failure of the two, but it is silent.\n\nIt also means the whole-workspace drain can never dedup a tree, only its blobs —\nconsistent with ADR-0061 s0's finding 3, and now with a cause naming s7 rather\nthan `head`-per-file.\n\nOptions, none of them free, all of them somebody's decision and not this ticket's:\n\n1. Two hashes: an **identity** hash over content+mode (what ADR-0027 compares) and\n   a **checkout** hash including mtimes (what a materialise reproduces). Correct,\n   and it doubles the tree vocabulary.\n2. Normalise mtimes on ingest (e.g. to the epoch, as reproducible-build tooling\n   does) and accept that incremental compilation across a Step boundary loses the\n   timestamps s7 restored — which is the thing s7 was written to fix.\n3. Keep mtimes and make ADR-0027's comparison structural (compare blob sets, not\n   root hashes).\n\nMeanwhile the live test has been narrowed to assert the part that still holds (the\nBLOB is identical across attempts) with a comment pointing here, so the knowledge\nis at the test site instead of in a deleted assertion.","files":null}]}